{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesfEAZ76Q7m6NdyTNG3i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete picture. Let me summarize the findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order.kt:11-16 — Order entity lacks status field\n- OrderController.kt:21-34 — POST /orders creates but no cancel endpoint\n- OrderRepository.kt:11-27 — In-memory store via ConcurrentHashMap\n- Shipment.kt:9-14 — Shipment has status enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27 — In-memory store, missing findByOrderId\n- ShipmentController.kt:26-44 — Creates shipments, no order status check\n- ApiExceptions.kt:19-24 — ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException\n- ApiError.kt:31-37 — ErrorCode enum, needs new code for cancel conflict\n- GlobalExceptionHandler.kt — Converts exceptions to error envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- HTTP status codes: 201 CREATED, 200 OK, 404 NOT_FOUND, 409 CONFLICT\n- Error response envelope: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [...]}}`\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException)\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions on both status and body\n- Repositories are in-memory with ConcurrentHashMap\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt — must add status field to Order\n2. OrderController.kt — must add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n3. OrderRepository.kt — no changes needed\n4. ShipmentRepository.kt — must add findByOrderId(orderId) method\n5. ShipmentController.kt — must check order status before creating shipment\n6. ApiError.kt — must add ORDER_CANCELLED_ERROR code\n7. OrderControllerTest.kt — must add cancel tests\n\n**Risks:**\n- Order status initialization for existing orders\n- Concurrent modifications during cancel\n- Shipment status transitions need proper semantics\n- All error cases must match the contract exactly\n\n**Open questions:** None—the ticket is clear on all cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` field with enum `OrderStatus { ACTIVE, CANCELLED }`. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order, throws 404 if not found\n   - If order is CANCELLED, returns 200 with order unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If order is ACTIVE, checks all shipments for that orderId\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throws 409 with new error code, changes nothing\n   - Otherwise, transitions order to CANCELLED and all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Returns the cancelled order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to fetch all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — In POST create(), check if the order exists and is not CANCELLED. If CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with new error code. If order doesn't exist, allow creation (current behavior).\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Add `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` error code for the 409 when shipment is CONFIRMED.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests for:\n   - Cancel active order returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancel cancels CREATED shipments\n   - Cancel already-cancelled order succeeds without changes\n   - Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancel unknown order returns 404\n   - Creating shipment for cancelled order returns 409\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered creating a separate `OrderService` layer, but the existing pattern has services inject repositories directly in controllers. Adding a service layer is unrelated refactoring and out of scope. The cancel logic is small enough to live in the controller.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Cancel active order:*\n- Read: Order by orderId, all Shipments by orderId\n- Validation: Order exists (404 if not), no CONFIRMED shipments (409 if yes)\n- Write: Update Order status to CANCELLED, update all CREATED Shipments to CANCELLED\n- Response: 200 with updated Order\n\n*Cancel already-cancelled order:*\n- Read: Order by orderId\n- Validation: Order exists (404 if not)\n- Response: 200 with Order, no writes\n\n*Create shipment for cancelled order:*\n- Read: Order by orderId\n- Validation: If Order exists and is CANCELLED, reject with 409\n- Response: 201 if success, 409 if CANCELLED, 201 if order not found\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. Test cancel ACTIVE order → 200, order CANCELLED, CREATED shipments CANCELLED\n2. Test cancel already CANCELLED order → 200, no changes\n3. Test cancel with CONFIRMED shipment → 409, no changes to order or shipments\n4. Test cancel unknown order → 404\n5. Test create shipment for CANCELLED order → 409\n6. Test create shipment for non-existent order → 201 (current behavior)\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll write the code and tests:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1939,"cache_read_input_tokens":17807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1939},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"654eb423-1112-4848-9096-98ba72a204a8","uuid":"0985aed8-aeb7-4546-a38f-541c899548c9","timestamp":"2026-09-09T09:52:16.769Z","request_id":"req_011CesfE9d3iPsfFg8fFq3u4"}
